\begin{aligned} f(3m) &= (3m)^{2} + 12 \\ &= 9m^{2} + 12. \end{aligned}
Next, we should plug in the range $(m)$ to the function, and then multiply by 3 to obtain a factor of 3. So,
\begin{aligned}
3(f(m)) &= 3(m^{2} + 12)\\
&= 3m^{2} + 3(12)\\
&= 3m^{2} + 36
\end{aligned}
Now we need to set the left and right sides of the expression equal to each other and solve for $m$. Thus,
\begin{aligned} f(3m) &=3(f(m)) \\ 9m^{2} + 12 &= 3m^{2} + 36 \\ 9m^{2} - 3m^{2} &= 36 - 12 \\ 6m^{2} &= 24 \\ m^{2} &= 4 \\ \sqrt{m^{2}} &= \sqrt{4} \\ m &= 2 \end{aligned}
Answer: 2.

